### 8. **Incorrect CORS Wildcard for No-Origin Requests (Lines 24-30 in server.js)**

```javascript
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (origin && ALLOWED_ORIGINS.has(origin)) {
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin);
  } else if (!origin) {
    // Same-origin or server-to-server (no Origin header)
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', '*');
  }
```

**Issue:** Line 30 sets `'*'` for missing Origin headers. This is overly permissive. Browsers will reject `*` if credentials are included, and this doesn't actually allow same-origin because same-origin requests don't send the Origin header. This should not set `*` — it should either set nothing or the actual request origin.

