### 10. **Missing Validation - requestBody.body Unchecked (Line 507 in server.js)**

```javascript
app.post('/api/config/project-dirs', (req, res) => {
  const { dirs } = req.body;
  if (!Array.isArray(dirs)) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'dirs must be an array' });
```

This validates the type but doesn't validate the array contents. An attacker could pass `[null, null, null, "../../etc/passwd"]` and if it's used in `path.resolve()` without further checks, it could cause issues. The code does validate with `path.resolve()` later (line 223), so this is lower risk.

